{"name":"Zydeco Blue","hex":"#2b61a0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zydeco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of Louisiana Creole music, characteristically performed by accordion and washboard bands, that combines Cajun and Creole roots music with elements of African-American music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zydeco"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zydeco","blocks":[{"text":"Zydeco is a music genre that was created in rural Southwest Louisiana by French-speaking African Americans of Creole heritage. It incorporates blues and rhythm and blues with music indigenous to the Louisiana Creoles, such as la la and juré. The main instruments are accordion and rubboard (washboard) or vest frottoir."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Buckwheat_Zydeco_and_band_performing_at_the_Kitchener_Blues_Festival.jpg/330px-Buckwheat_Zydeco_and_band_performing_at_the_Kitchener_Blues_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zydeco","wikidata":"Q245296"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Zydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg/500px-Zydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Zydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg/1280px-Zydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Zydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg/500px-Zydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"New Orleans Cajun-Zydeco Fest, 2019","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZydeco_fest_in_New_Orleans_2018.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Zydeco_players_Louisiana_1938.jpg/500px-Zydeco_players_Louisiana_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Zydeco_players_Louisiana_1938.jpg/1280px-Zydeco_players_Louisiana_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Zydeco_players_Louisiana_1938.jpg/500px-Zydeco_players_Louisiana_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early Creole musicians playing an accordion and a washboard in front of a store, near Opelousa